now to our exclusive interview with  urban magic johnson one of the greatest  basketball players of all time nate just  told us he's his favorite player he won  five nba titles with the la lakers an  olympic gold medal with the 1992 dream  team 30 years ago this week johnson  revealed at a press conference that he  had hiv the virus that can cause aids  the news was a bombshell because at the  time that diagnosis was considered a  death sentence we spoke with johnson at  the waldorf historian los angeles about  his reaction that day and how he got  through it with the support of his wife  cookie  even for hollywood it was perfect  casting the man who single-handedly  produced magical moments on the  basketball court was at the top of his  game when it all disappeared right  before our eyes  a tragic ending to a magical career  because of the  hiv virus that i have attained  i will have to retire from the lakers  let's go back urban 30 years what did  you know about hiv before you were  diagnosed  because what we knew was scary right at  that time  the only thing i knew  if you got aids you you died right and  so i had to really learn a lot about the  disease  hiv as well as aids  had to make sure that  i was open-minded enough to ask a lot of  questions  go get a lot of information from  different people johnson first learned  of his diagnosis after a routine  physical back in 1991.  he was called back home from a preseason  game in utah so that the lakers team  physician dr michael mellman could  deliver the news in person  went straight to dr melman's office and  then that's when he told me  i had hiv and when you first heard those  words what was the thought in your mind  oh i was just devastated i'm asking them  a hundred times are you sure  they say hey we ran the test a couple of  times and  yes you do have hiv  and so i just  lost it right there you know you just  sit there and say what does this mean  am i going to die because i definitely  asked him that  and he said well  you have a chance to live for a long  time with all the new drugs that are  coming down the pipeline but the  toughest thing gail that i had to do was  really drive home and tell cookie it was  hard because i loved her so much and i  and i hated to hurt her  i played against some of the best  basketball players in the world right  i've been in championships i've been in  nine finals so i know pressure  but it was no greater pressure than  driving home to tell her even today is  still the toughest thing i've ever had  to do in my life the johnsons were  married a little over a month when magic  announced his diagnosis and they had  just learned cookie was pregnant the key  moment was when cookie  took the test and the results came back  that her and the baby was fine that was  a huge relief yes yes because i was  scared to death i wanted to make sure  that she was going to be okay the baby  was going to be okay and then i could  move forward with trying to make sure i  was going to be okay irvine magic  johnson attacked the stigma surrounding  hiv with the same passion he displayed  on the court launching the magic johnson  foundation to raise awareness about the  virus then pushing congress and the  white house to spend money to fight the  disease but he's still long for the game  of basketball and his first retirement  would be short-lived even though he had  not played a single regular season game  fans voted him onto the nba all-star  team in 1992 and a few months later he  played on the u.s olympic dream team  it proved to be the right decision  it helped people who were living with  not just hiv and aids but with  any disease that you can live on you can  be and live a productive life  there were mixed reviews about you  coming back controversy over johnson's  return has erupted in the last few weeks  even one of his olympic dream teammates  carl malone expressed fear about having  to play against him in the physical  sometimes bloody nba arena how did you  feel when there was backlash about you  returning with some of the players when  you got hurt yeah i got cut  and i was very upset  at the backlash because i just played  with a lot of the guys who  didn't want me to come back yeah you  know well i just spent three months with  you  playing against you with you  and so now but you got cutting that  changed again  that scared people that scared the crowd  you could just hear  i never want to hurt the game right  so this is a game that i love  and so  if the guys are going to be scared the  fans didn't know so i said you know what  after that game i said i'm just going to  retire johnson returned to the sport he  loved one more time in 1996. i told  cookie i said you know what  maybe i should look at playing one more  time because i want to end it the right  way okay because you never felt it it  ended the right way exactly okay and  that's why i came back i ended it the  way i wanted  it to end after that his focus finally  began to shift oh i missed the game oh  man cookie will tell you  i sit on that couch and watching the  lakers play that was so hard for me you  know because i said i should be out  there  but it wasn't until she came home i tell  you  gail what changed my life and got me  going into business she came home and  said you know what ervin  i'm  mad and i'm upset  you got to be the man that i married  and i  i was like oh my goodness  like you've always wanted to be in  business why are you sitting on this  couch wow  you got to get started so  get out cookie johnson remembers that  moment too  i'm looking at you like this sitting on  this couch that's not the man i married  you know the man i married was a hard  worker  he was changing the world you know he  had all these ideas he had he was so  full of life  i don't know who this is  and you need to get up and figure that  out  irvin and cookie met when they were  students at michigan state university in  the 70s cookie says at first she did not  want to have the press conference  announcing his diagnosis the stigma with  aids at that time people weren't  educated so they thought you couldn't  touch people you couldn't hug people  and i didn't want people to treat us  like we were lepers i still remember the  press conference you're sitting there  that white suit what were you thinking  i was thinking you know be strong and i  wore that white suit for a reason i  didn't want to wear anything dark or  black because to me it's what it  symbolized and the white suit to me  symbolized you know brightness like a  future basically  you know positivity  when he told you how he got it what was  your thought at that time when he said  you know that he had it and it was  probably through sexual context because  he didn't have any blood transfusions or  anything like that it wasn't how he got  it that was important to me  it was  you're possibly going to die  and that trumped everything she really  is a living example irving of for better  or worse in the marriage vows right  don't you think no no  because for some people for better or  worse doesn't include that right you  know right even when we broke up all  those times and i was dating other  people i said i'm gonna make i already  know who i'm a married you did oh i told  all the women that i know who i'm gonna  marry  i bet you were a fun date  i'm really gonna marry her oh oh they  knew they knew what they knew i was  gonna marry cookie there's no doubt who  i was gonna marry with cookie by his  side the 62 year old basketball legend  is a very successful businessman a  loving father and grandfather don't you  feel like this is your city this is my i  do i feel it's your city oh yeah oh yeah  today johnson runs point in the  boardroom as ceo of magic johnson  enterprises  an investment company focused on  providing high quality products and  services to underserved communities do i  dare ask if being a businessman  entrepreneur philanthropist  is better than playing basketball yes  is it better yes it is and how is your  health today oh it's great  still undetectable and so  you have to take medication every day  still yes still cocktail once a day it  went from three times a day now just  once  and so  everything is great andy says no matter  what there's one thing his diagnosis  decades ago could never defeat  that situation wasn't going to change  my attitude and mindset and the person  that i am okay if if i was gonna die i  was gonna die being irving johnson right  and what does that mean being i mean  just being an upbeat person with a good  attitude  um and so  that's just who i am  that is exactly who he is he said most  people said he wouldn't last three or  four years let alone 30. as you see he  certainly credits cookie he says if it  wasn't for cookie i wouldn't be the man  i was today i say here here to that he's  a hero but she certainly is a hero in a  very other way he he admits that without  her he wouldn't have gotten through this  and after that news conference where you  know as you as you heard she didn't want  to have it a group of friends took them  to hawaii so they could just be alone  and they said we'll never forget how we  were embraced at that time it's a  beautiful thing and what an example of  making a marriage work right uh and the  courage there from from magic johnson  you forget in that in that moment rock  hudson the great hollywood actor had  just died five years earlier very  publicly and people really really felt  if you have this you're done yeah  individuals like arthur ashe as well  because of the transfusion um i i think  about kobe bryant because it happened  recently another laker player but it  just rocked sports fans to the core that  he passed away along with the others on  that helicopter it was kind of like that  for magic johnson yeah because we just  all assumed one of the greatest players  is going to die yeah and he's still here  we're happy to say he gets up at 4 30  every day and goes to the gym he's still  working out taking his medication he's  all good and a great businessman too and  a really good businessman knows how to  make money in addition to the magic  johnson foundation you can find  information on hiv testing prevention  and treatment by visiting hiv.gov  gov

